DTSTART:20261126T063000
DTEND:20261126T063500
SUMMARY:Day 1 Morning: The count begins
DESCRIPTION:Week 1: See It. You can't fix what you won't count.\n\nToday y
 ou only count. Every lie\, every exaggeration\, every "yeah\, I did" that 
 wasn't true. No fixing\, no beating yourself up. Keep a tally in your phon
 e notes as it happens.\n\nHOW TO DO IT\n1. Before you leave the house\, ma
 ke a note on your phone called "Truth Ledger" and pin it.\n2. Every time y
 ou say something untrue\, add a tally mark right away. If you can't stop\,
  add it at your next break.\n3. Count everything: exaggerations\, "I'm alm
 ost there\," pretending to remember\, fake reasons\, and lies of leaving s
 omething out.\n4. Don't fix or correct anything today. The only job is to 
 see clearly.\n(Full instructions: "The nightly ledger" in How to practice\
 , in your guide.)\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happen
 s\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Tracking your behavior changes yo
 ur behavior. The nightly ledger is the written record\, and the weekly rev
 iew compares your numbers week to week. You can also enter your three numb
 ers on each day in this guide. (Harkin et al. (2016)\, Psychological Bulle
 tin)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 1 Morning: The count begins
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
