UID:truth-ledger-6@bethemansystem.com
DTSTAMP:20261125T142333Z
DTSTART:20261128T063000
DTEND:20261128T063500
SUMMARY:Day 3 Morning: Where and when
DESCRIPTION:Week 1: See It. You can't fix what you won't count.\n\nNote wh
 ere you are and what time it is each time you lie today: at home\, at work
 \, on the phone\, by text\, tired\, rushed\, after a mistake.\n\nHOW TO DO
  IT\n1. Each time you lie\, add a word for where you were (home\, work\, c
 ar\, phone\, text) and the time.\n2. Also note your state: tired\, rushed\
 , hungry\, stressed\, or fine.\n3. Tonight\, circle the three situations t
 hat show up most. Write them on the first page of your ledger. You'll use 
 them all program.\n(Full instructions: "The nightly ledger" in How to prac
 tice\, in your guide.)\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ h
 appens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: You can do CBT on your own. 
 Doing it alone works if you keep showing up. The daily reminders and the n
 ightly ledger are your structure. The biggest risk is quitting\, so the pl
 an is built around never missing two nights in a row. (Karyotaki et al. (2
 017)\, JAMA Psychiatry)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 3 Morning: Where and when
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
