BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:truth-ledger-9@bethemansystem.com
DTSTAMP:20261125T142333Z
DTSTART:20261129T063000
DTEND:20261129T063500
SUMMARY:Day 4 Morning: Who gets the lies
DESCRIPTION:Week 1: See It. You can't fix what you won't count.\n\nNotice 
 who you lie to most. Write their names as it happens: wife\, boss\, kids\,
  friends\, parents\, yourself.\n\nHOW TO DO IT\n1. Each time you lie\, add
  the person's name or role.\n2. Notice whether you lie more to people you 
 want to impress\, people you're afraid of\, or people closest to you.\n3. 
 Tonight\, rank the names from most lies to fewest.\n(Full instructions: "T
 he nightly ledger" in How to practice\, in your guide.)\n\nBefore you go\,
  write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it wo
 rks: Trying to look competent or likable makes people lie more. Your two f
 ears\, failing and not being accepted\, are exactly these two goals. Week 
 2 teaches you to notice which one is running in the moment. (Feldman\, For
 rest & Happ (2002)\, Basic and Applied Social Psychology)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 4 Morning: Who gets the lies
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
