UID:truth-ledger-12@bethemansystem.com
DTSTAMP:20261125T142333Z
DTSTART:20261130T063000
DTEND:20261130T063500
SUMMARY:Day 5 Morning: The alarm in your body
DESCRIPTION:Week 1: See It. You can't fix what you won't count.\n\nNotice 
 what your body does right before a lie: tight chest\, hot face\, dry throa
 t\, talking faster. That feeling is your alarm. Learn it today.\n\nHOW TO 
 DO IT\n1. The next three times you feel the urge to lie\, stop and scan yo
 ur body from head to stomach.\n2. Write what you notice in two or three wo
 rds: "hot face\," "tight chest\," "fast talking."\n3. Count\, roughly\, ho
 w many seconds pass between the feeling and the words. That gap is where t
 he pause will go.\n(Full instructions: "The three-second pause" in How to 
 practice\, in your guide.)\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If _
 __ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Break an automatic habit
 : notice it\, then replace it. Day 5 teaches you your body's alarm. The pa
 use and a prepared true sentence (Week 4) are the replacement response. (B
 ate\, Malouff\, Thorsteinsson & Bhullar (2011)\, Clinical Psychology Revie
 w (meta-analysis))
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 5 Morning: The alarm in your body
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
