SUMMARY:Day 7 Morning: Week 1 review
DESCRIPTION:Week 1: See It. You can't fix what you won't count.\n\nKeep co
 unting today. Tonight is your first weekly review.\n\nHOW TO DO IT\n1. Kee
 p counting all day.\n2. Tonight\, add up the week from your ledger: total 
 told\, caught and corrected.\n3. Find your worst day and write three thing
 s that were different about it (sleep\, stress\, people\, place).\n4. Writ
 e one sentence about what you learned this week.\n(Full instructions: "The
  nightly ledger" in How to practice\, in your guide.)\n\nBefore you go\, w
 rite today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it work
 s: Tracking your behavior changes your behavior. The nightly ledger is the
  written record\, and the weekly review compares your numbers week to week
 . You can also enter your three numbers on each day in this guide. (Harkin
  et al. (2016)\, Psychological Bulletin)
