SUMMARY:Day 8 Morning: The fear of failing
DESCRIPTION:Week 2: The Fear Underneath. Every lie is protecting something
 .\n\nEach time you feel the urge to lie today\, ask yourself: "Am I hiding
  that I failed?"\n\nHOW TO DO IT\n1. Each time you feel the urge to lie\, 
 ask yourself silently: "Am I hiding that I failed?"\n2. If yes\, mark the 
 lie with an F in your ledger.\n3. Tonight\, count the Fs.\n(Full instructi
 ons: "The nightly ledger" in How to practice\, in your guide.)\n\nBefore y
 ou go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWh
 y it works: Trying to look competent or likable makes people lie more. You
 r two fears\, failing and not being accepted\, are exactly these two goals
 . Week 2 teaches you to notice which one is running in the moment. (Feldma
 n\, Forrest & Happ (2002)\, Basic and Applied Social Psychology)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 8 Morning: The fear of failing
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
