SUMMARY:Day 9 Morning: The fear of not being accepted
DESCRIPTION:Week 2: The Fear Underneath. Every lie is protecting something
 .\n\nEach time the urge hits\, ask yourself: "Am I trying to be liked righ
 t now?"\n\nHOW TO DO IT\n1. Each time you feel the urge\, ask yourself sil
 ently: "Am I trying to be liked right now?"\n2. If yes\, mark the lie with
  an L.\n3. Tonight\, do the sentence exercise fast\, without stopping to t
 hink. Write all ten endings.\n(Full instructions: "The nightly ledger" in 
 How to practice\, in your guide.)\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then
 : "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Trying to look co
 mpetent or likable makes people lie more. Your two fears\, failing and not
  being accepted\, are exactly these two goals. Week 2 teaches you to notic
 e which one is running in the moment. (Feldman\, Forrest & Happ (2002)\, B
 asic and Applied Social Psychology)
