SUMMARY:Day 10 Morning: Where it started
DESCRIPTION:Week 2: The Fear Underneath. Every lie is protecting something
 .\n\nAt some point today\, think back to the first time you remember lying
  to stay safe. Who were you protecting yourself from?\n\nHOW TO DO IT\n1. 
 Sometime today\, set a 10-minute timer and think back. Who did you lie to 
 as a kid\, and what were you afraid would happen?\n2. Write the memory dow
 n in a few sentences: your age\, where you were\, who it was.\n3. Tonight\
 , write the boy a letter of at least five sentences. Start with "I know wh
 y you did it."\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\,
  then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Writing about hard things helps a li
 ttle. The evening questions and letters are writing exercises. They help\,
  but they're one tool among several\, not a cure. (Frattaroli (2006)\, Psy
 chological Bulletin)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 10 Morning: Where it started
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
