UID:truth-ledger-37@bethemansystem.com
DTSTAMP:20261125T142333Z
DTSTART:20261208T063000
DTEND:20261208T063500
SUMMARY:Day 13 Morning: Test your prediction
DESCRIPTION:Week 2: The Fear Underneath. Every lie is protecting something
 .\n\nRun an experiment. Before one true thing you'd normally lie about tod
 ay\, write your prediction first: "If I say it\, ___ will happen." Then sa
 y it.\n\nHOW TO DO IT\n1. This morning\, pick one small truth you'd normal
 ly lie about today.\n2. Before you say it\, write your prediction: "If I s
 ay it\, ___ will happen." Rate your fear from 0 to 10.\n3. Say the truth.\
 n4. Right after\, write what actually happened and rate your fear again.\n
 (Full instructions: "Rating fear and urges from 0 to 10" in How to practic
 e\, in your guide.)\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happ
 ens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Lies are safety behaviors. Drop
 ping them teaches you that the truth is survivable. Each lie you don't tel
 l is a test of your prediction. The prediction test (Day 13) and the truth
  ladder (Week 5) are behavioral experiments. (Clark & Wells cognitive mode
 l\; Morgan & Raffle (1999)\; Salkovskis)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 13 Morning: Test your prediction
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
