 Lies told today (#): what\, to whom\n2. Lies caught before I spoke (#)\n3.
  Corrections made (#)\n4. The trigger: who\, where\, how tired I was\, and
  the fear (failure / rejection / conflict / looking weak)\n5. The story in
  my head: "If I tell the truth\, ___ will happen."\n6. What actually happe
 ned when I told the truth\n7. Tomorrow's risk moment\, written as an if-th
 en: "If ___\, then I'll say ___."\n8. One line of prayer or thanks
