SUMMARY:Day 14 Morning: Week 2 review: your Fear Map
DESCRIPTION:Week 2: The Fear Underneath. Every lie is protecting something
 .\n\nToday\, draw your Fear Map: your top three fears\, the lie each one p
 roduces\, and the truth each one avoids.\n\nHOW TO DO IT\n1. Make three co
 lumns on one page: My fear | The lie it makes me tell | The truth I'm avoi
 ding.\n2. Fill in one row for each of your top three fears\, using your le
 dger from the last two weeks.\n3. Keep this page. It's your Fear Map\, and
  you'll come back to it.\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___
  happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Lies are safety behaviors.
  Dropping them teaches you that the truth is survivable. Each lie you don'
 t tell is a test of your prediction. The prediction test (Day 13) and the 
 truth ladder (Week 5) are behavioral experiments. (Clark & Wells cognitive
  model\; Morgan & Raffle (1999)\; Salkovskis)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 14 Morning: Week 2 review: your Fear Map
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
