UID:truth-ledger-47@bethemansystem.com
DTSTAMP:20261125T142333Z
DTSTART:20261211T063000
DTEND:20261211T063500
SUMMARY:Day 16 Morning: Ride the urge
DESCRIPTION:Week 3: The Pause. Lies are fast. Truth needs three seconds.\n
 \nWhen the urge to lie hits today\, don't act on it right away. Rate it fr
 om 0 to 10 and watch it. Urges rise\, peak and fade\, usually within a min
 ute or two.\n\nHOW TO DO IT\n1. The first time the urge hits today\, don't
  answer for a moment. Use the pause.\n2. Rate the urge from 0 to 10 and no
 tice where it is in your body.\n3. Breathe slowly and watch it for one to 
 two minutes\, or as long as the moment allows.\n4. Rate it again. Write bo
 th numbers in your ledger.\n(Full instructions: "Riding the urge" in How t
 o practice\, in your guide.)\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If
  ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: A slip doesn't have to
  become a relapse. If you lie\, you correct it\, log it\, and keep going. 
 You never go back to Day 1. (Marlatt & Gordon\, Relapse Prevention\; Larim
 er\, Palmer & Marlatt (1999))
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 16 Morning: Ride the urge
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
