UID:truth-ledger-50@bethemansystem.com
DTSTAMP:20261125T142333Z
DTSTART:20261212T063000
DTEND:20261212T063500
SUMMARY:Day 17 Morning: "I don't know"
DESCRIPTION:Week 3: The Pause. Lies are fast. Truth needs three seconds.\n
 \nSay "I don't know" or "I'm not sure" at least once today instead of fill
 ing the silence with something you made up.\n\nHOW TO DO IT\n1. Decide thi
 s morning: at least once today\, when you don't know something\, you'll sa
 y "I don't know" or "I'm not sure."\n2. Watch for moments where you'd norm
 ally guess\, bluff or pretend to remember.\n3. Say it plainly\, with no ap
 ology after it.\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\
 , then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Lies are safety behaviors. Dropping
  them teaches you that the truth is survivable. Each lie you don't tell is
  a test of your prediction. The prediction test (Day 13) and the truth lad
 der (Week 5) are behavioral experiments. (Clark & Wells cognitive model\; 
 Morgan & Raffle (1999)\; Salkovskis)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 17 Morning: "I don't know"
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
