DTSTART:20261213T063000
DTEND:20261213T063500
SUMMARY:Day 18 Morning: The 60-second correction
DESCRIPTION:Week 3: The Pause. Lies are fast. Truth needs three seconds.\n
 \nIf a lie slips out\, correct it inside a minute: "Actually\, that's not 
 true. The truth is ___." Fast correction beats a perfect record.\n\nHOW TO
  DO IT\n1. Memorize the words: "Actually\, that's not true. The truth is _
 __."\n2. When a lie slips out\, say them inside a minute. Don't explain.\n
 3. If you miss the window\, correct it before the end of the day.\n4. Log 
 every correction tonight.\n(Full instructions: "The correction" in How to 
 practice\, in your guide.)\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If _
 __ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: A slip doesn't have to b
 ecome a relapse. If you lie\, you correct it\, log it\, and keep going. Yo
 u never go back to Day 1. (Marlatt & Gordon\, Relapse Prevention\; Larimer
 \, Palmer & Marlatt (1999))
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 18 Morning: The 60-second correction
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
