DTSTAMP:20261125T142333Z
DTSTART:20261214T063000
DTEND:20261214T063500
SUMMARY:Day 19 Morning: Slow down
DESCRIPTION:Week 3: The Pause. Lies are fast. Truth needs three seconds.\n
 \nIn every hard conversation today\, speak about 20% slower. Rushing feeds
  lies.\n\nHOW TO DO IT\n1. Before any conversation that matters today\, te
 ll yourself: "Slow."\n2. Speak at about 80% of your normal speed. Leave a 
 full breath before answering a question.\n3. Notice any moment where slowi
 ng down changed your answer.\n(Full instructions: "The three-second pause"
  in How to practice\, in your guide.)\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-
 then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: The pause int
 errupts an automatic response. The three-second pause isn't magic. It's th
 e gap where your prepared true sentence gets a chance. (Kobis et al. (2019
 )\, Perspectives on Psychological Science\; Curtis & Hart (2020))
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 19 Morning: Slow down
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
