DESCRIPTION:Tonight's question: Where did slowing down change what came ou
 t of your mouth?\n\nTHE LEDGER (10 min)\n1. Lies told today (#): what\, to
  whom\n2. Lies caught before I spoke (#)\n3. Corrections made (#)\n4. The 
 trigger: who\, where\, how tired I was\, and the fear (failure / rejection
  / conflict / looking weak)\n5. The story in my head: "If I tell the truth
 \, ___ will happen."\n6. What actually happened when I told the truth\n7. 
 Tomorrow's risk moment\, written as an if-then: "If ___\, then I'll say __
