BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:truth-ledger-59@bethemansystem.com
DTSTAMP:20261125T142333Z
DTSTART:20261215T063000
DTEND:20261215T063500
SUMMARY:Day 20 Morning: No rounding up
DESCRIPTION:Week 3: The Pause. Lies are fast. Truth needs three seconds.\n
 \nToday\, nothing gets inflated: not numbers\, times\, effort or stories. 
 Small lies make the brain's alarm quieter\, which makes the next lie bigge
 r. Exact is the goal.\n\nHOW TO DO IT\n1. Today\, every number is exact: t
 imes\, money\, miles\, how many\, how long.\n2. No "almost done\," "five m
 inutes away" or "a few" unless it's literally true.\n3. When you catch you
 rself rounding up\, correct it on the spot: "Actually\, it's closer to ___
 ."\n(Full instructions: "The correction" in How to practice\, in your guid
 e.)\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll 
 say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Small lies make bigger lies easier. There's no 
 such thing as a harmless small lie for you. Every exaggeration trains the 
 slope. That's why Day 20 is "No rounding up." (Garrett\, Lazzaro\, Ariely 
 & Sharot (2016)\, Nature Neuroscience)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 20 Morning: No rounding up
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
