BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:truth-ledger-72@bethemansystem.com
DTSTAMP:20261125T142333Z
DTSTART:20261219T063000
DTEND:20261219T063500
SUMMARY:Day 24 Morning: Say the feeling instead
DESCRIPTION:Week 4: Replace the Lie. You can't just stop. You have to say 
 something else.\n\nMany lies stand in for feelings. Today\, when the urge 
 hits\, name the feeling instead\, out loud or to yourself: "I'm embarrasse
 d." "I'm afraid I'll look bad."\n\nHOW TO DO IT\n1. When the urge hits tod
 ay\, before anything else\, name the feeling underneath it: embarrassed\, 
 afraid\, ashamed\, guilty\, tired.\n2. Say it to yourself in a full senten
 ce: "I'm embarrassed that I forgot."\n3. If it's safe and useful\, say the
  feeling out loud to the person instead of the lie.\n4. Log each feeling y
 ou named tonight.\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happen
 s\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Writing about hard things helps a
  little. The evening questions and letters are writing exercises. They hel
 p\, but they're one tool among several\, not a cure. (Frattaroli (2006)\, 
 Psychological Bulletin)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 24 Morning: Say the feeling instead
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
