UID:truth-ledger-75@bethemansystem.com
DTSTAMP:20261125T142333Z
DTSTART:20261220T063000
DTEND:20261220T063500
SUMMARY:Day 25 Morning: Private is not a lie
DESCRIPTION:Week 4: Replace the Lie. You can't just stop. You have to say 
 something else.\n\nYou're allowed to not share something. "I'd rather not 
 get into that" is honest. Making something up is not. Today\, when you wan
 t to hide something\, decline instead of inventing.\n\nHOW TO DO IT\n1. Le
 arn the difference: declining ("I'd rather not talk about that") is honest
 . Making something up is lying.\n2. Today\, when you want to hide somethin
 g\, decline instead of inventing a story.\n3. Tonight\, review what you ke
 pt private. Ask yourself honestly: does this affect someone else's life\, 
 money or safety? If yes\, it isn't just private. Add it to your list of tr
 uths to tell.\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, 
 then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: If-then plans work. Every morning you
  write one if-then plan for the day's risk moment: "If she asks about the 
 money\, then I'll say the real number." (Gollwitzer & Sheeran (2006)\, Adv
 ances in Experimental Social Psychology)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 25 Morning: Private is not a lie
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:truth-ledger-76@bethemansystem.com
DTSTAMP:20261125T142333Z
DTSTART:20261220T123000
DTEND:20261220T123500
