BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:truth-ledger-78@bethemansystem.com
DTSTAMP:20261125T142333Z
DTSTART:20261221T063000
DTEND:20261221T063500
SUMMARY:Day 26 Morning: No made-up excuses
DESCRIPTION:Week 4: Replace the Lie. You can't just stop. You have to say 
 something else.\n\nWhen you're late\, forget or fall short today\, state t
 he fact with no invented reason: "I'm late. I left late." "I forgot."\n\nH
 OW TO DO IT\n1. Whenever you're late\, forget or fall short today\, say th
 e fact only: "I'm late." "I forgot." "I didn't finish."\n2. Don't invent t
 raffic\, a dead battery or someone else's fault.\n3. If there's a real rea
 son\, you can give it\, but only if it's true and only after the fact.\n\n
 Before you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___
 ."\n\nWhy it works: Lies are safety behaviors. Dropping them teaches you t
 hat the truth is survivable. Each lie you don't tell is a test of your pre
 diction. The prediction test (Day 13) and the truth ladder (Week 5) are be
 havioral experiments. (Clark & Wells cognitive model\; Morgan & Raffle (19
 99)\; Salkovskis)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 26 Morning: No made-up excuses
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
