DTEND:20261222T063500
SUMMARY:Day 27 Morning: When you're tired
DESCRIPTION:Week 4: Replace the Lie. You can't just stop. You have to say 
 something else.\n\nLook at your ledger: lies often come when you're tired\
 , rushed or stressed. Write an if-then for tonight: "If I'm worn out and s
 omeone asks me something\, then I'll say: let me answer that in the mornin
 g."\n\nHOW TO DO IT\n1. Look back at your ledger. Find the time of day whe
 n you lie most. That's your danger zone.\n2. Write one if-then plan for th
 at time: "If it's after 8pm and I'm asked something I don't want to answer
 \, then I say: let me answer that in the morning."\n3. Tonight\, notice ho
 w tired you are on a 0 to 10 scale before your ledger\, and write it down.
 \n(Full instructions: "If-then plans" in How to practice\, in your guide.)
 \n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say
  ___."\n\nWhy it works: Tired men have less self-control. Treat being tire
 d as a risk factor. Your evening ledger and your relapse warning signs inc
 lude sleep. (Barnes\, Schaubroeck\, Huth & Ghumman (2011)\, Organizational
  Behavior and Human Decision Processes)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 27 Morning: When you're tired
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
