SUMMARY:Day 28 Morning: Week 4 review
DESCRIPTION:Week 4: Replace the Lie. You can't just stop. You have to say 
 something else.\n\nRead all your if-then plans this morning.\n\nHOW TO DO 
 IT\n1. This morning\, read all your if-then plans out loud once.\n2. Tonig
 ht\, mark each plan: Worked\, Didn't come up\, or Failed.\n3. Rewrite ever
 y plan that failed so it's shorter or more specific.\n(Full instructions: 
 "If-then plans" in How to practice\, in your guide.)\n\nBefore you go\, wr
 ite today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works
 : Tracking your behavior changes your behavior. The nightly ledger is the 
 written record\, and the weekly review compares your numbers week to week.
  You can also enter your three numbers on each day in this guide. (Harkin 
 et al. (2016)\, Psychological Bulletin)
