DTSTART:20261224T063000
DTEND:20261224T063500
SUMMARY:Day 29 Morning: Build your truth ladder
DESCRIPTION:Week 5: Small Truths\, Out Loud. Courage is a muscle. Train it
  light first.\n\nList ten truths you've been avoiding\, from easiest ("I'm
  running late") to hardest. Today\, tell the easiest one.\n\nHOW TO DO IT\
 n1. Set aside 20 minutes. Build your truth ladder using the instructions i
 n How to practice.\n2. Pick rung 1\, the easiest truth. Write your fear ra
 ting and your prediction.\n3. Say it today.\n4. Write your fear rating aft
 erward and what actually happened.\n(Full instructions: "The truth ladder"
  in How to practice\, in your guide.)\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-
 then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Lies are safe
 ty behaviors. Dropping them teaches you that the truth is survivable. Each
  lie you don't tell is a test of your prediction. The prediction test (Day
  13) and the truth ladder (Week 5) are behavioral experiments. (Clark & We
 lls cognitive model\; Morgan & Raffle (1999)\; Salkovskis)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 29 Morning: Build your truth ladder
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
