SUMMARY:Day 30 Morning: An honest no
DESCRIPTION:Week 5: Small Truths\, Out Loud. Courage is a muscle. Train it
  light first.\n\nSay one honest "no" or "I can't" today with no made-up ex
 cuse attached.\n\nHOW TO DO IT\n1. Pick one request today that you'd norma
 lly dodge with an excuse.\n2. Say "No" or "I can't" with no made-up reason
 . If there's a true reason\, give it in one sentence.\n3. Rate your fear b
 efore and after.\n(Full instructions: "Rating fear and urges from 0 to 10"
  in How to practice\, in your guide.)\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-
 then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Lies are safe
 ty behaviors. Dropping them teaches you that the truth is survivable. Each
  lie you don't tell is a test of your prediction. The prediction test (Day
  13) and the truth ladder (Week 5) are behavioral experiments. (Clark & We
 lls cognitive model\; Morgan & Raffle (1999)\; Salkovskis)
