UID:truth-ledger-94@bethemansystem.com
DTSTAMP:20261125T142333Z
DTSTART:20261226T063000
DTEND:20261226T063500
SUMMARY:Day 31 Morning: Admit it first
DESCRIPTION:Week 5: Small Truths\, Out Loud. Courage is a muscle. Train it
  light first.\n\nBefore anyone finds out\, admit one small mistake today: 
 "That was me. I'll fix it."\n\nHOW TO DO IT\n1. Think of one small mistake
  you made recently that nobody has noticed yet.\n2. Before anyone finds ou
 t\, say: "That was me. Here's what I'll do to fix it."\n3. Then do the fix
 .\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll sa
 y ___."\n\nWhy it works: Shame hides. Guilt repairs. Day 11 teaches you to
  turn shame sentences into guilt sentences. You can repair something you d
 id. You can't repair who you are. (Tangney & Dearing\, Shame and Guilt (20
 02) and later reviews)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 31 Morning: Admit it first
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
