SUMMARY:Day 32 Morning: Climb a rung
DESCRIPTION:Week 5: Small Truths\, Out Loud. Courage is a muscle. Train it
  light first.\n\nTell rung three or four of your ladder today.\n\nHOW TO D
 O IT\n1. Pick rung 3 or 4 of your ladder.\n2. Write your prediction and fe
 ar rating.\n3. Say it today.\n4. Write what happened and your fear rating 
 afterward.\n(Full instructions: "The truth ladder" in How to practice\, in
  your guide.)\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, 
 then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Lies are safety behaviors. Dropping t
 hem teaches you that the truth is survivable. Each lie you don't tell is a
  test of your prediction. The prediction test (Day 13) and the truth ladde
 r (Week 5) are behavioral experiments. (Clark & Wells cognitive model\; Mo
 rgan & Raffle (1999)\; Salkovskis)
