DTEND:20261228T063500
SUMMARY:Day 33 Morning: Take the reaction
DESCRIPTION:Week 5: Small Truths\, Out Loud. Courage is a muscle. Train it
  light first.\n\nBefore a hard truth today\, take two minutes to write abo
 ut what matters most to you: your faith\, your children\, the man you've d
 ecided to be. Then\, when the truth gets a reaction\, don't defend\, expla
 in or lie again.\n\nHOW TO DO IT\n1. Before your hardest truth today\, set
  a 2-minute timer.\n2. Write about one thing that matters most to you (you
 r faith\, your children\, the man you've decided to be) and why.\n3. Then 
 tell the truth. If the person reacts with anger or hurt\, don't defend or 
 explain. Say "I understand" and let it land.\n4. Log what you wanted to sa
 y in your defense\, and what you said instead.\n(Full instructions: "The t
 ruth ladder" in How to practice\, in your guide.)\n\nBefore you go\, write
  today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: R
 emembering your values makes you less defensive. Before a hard truth\, spe
 nd two minutes writing about what matters most to you: your faith\, your c
 hildren\, the man you've decided to be (Day 33). (Sherman & Cohen (2002)\,
  Current Directions in Psychological Science)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 33 Morning: Take the reaction
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
