SUMMARY:Day 34 Morning: Climb again
DESCRIPTION:Week 5: Small Truths\, Out Loud. Courage is a muscle. Train it
  light first.\n\nTell rung five or six of your ladder today.\n\nHOW TO DO 
 IT\n1. Pick rung 5 or 6 of your ladder.\n2. Write your prediction and fear
  rating.\n3. Say it today.\n4. Compare: what you predicted versus what hap
 pened. Write the gap.\n(Full instructions: "The truth ladder" in How to pr
 actice\, in your guide.)\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___
  happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Lies are safety behaviors.
  Dropping them teaches you that the truth is survivable. Each lie you don'
 t tell is a test of your prediction. The prediction test (Day 13) and the 
 truth ladder (Week 5) are behavioral experiments. (Clark & Wells cognitive
  model\; Morgan & Raffle (1999)\; Salkovskis)
