SUMMARY:Day 35 Morning: Week 5 review
DESCRIPTION:Week 5: Small Truths\, Out Loud. Courage is a muscle. Train it
  light first.\n\nLook at your ladder. Mark every rung you've climbed.\n\nH
 OW TO DO IT\n1. Look at your ladder and mark every rung you've climbed.\n2
 . For each one\, write the fear rating before and after.\n3. Tonight\, add
  up the week. Write the truth that you feared most and what really happene
 d.\n(Full instructions: "The truth ladder" in How to practice\, in your gu
 ide.)\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'l
 l say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Tracking your behavior changes your behavior.
  The nightly ledger is the written record\, and the weekly review compares
  your numbers week to week. You can also enter your three numbers on each 
 day in this guide. (Harkin et al. (2016)\, Psychological Bulletin)
