DTSTAMP:20261125T142333Z
DTSTART:20270101T063000
DTEND:20270101T063500
SUMMARY:Day 37 Morning: Work
DESCRIPTION:Week 6: Hard Truths. Tell the truth where it costs the most.\n
 \nAt work today\, no inflating your progress and no excuses for what isn't
  done. Report exactly where things stand.\n\nHOW TO DO IT\n1. At work toda
 y\, report status exactly: done\, not done\, or how far along.\n2. No "alm
 ost\," no "on it" when you haven't started.\n3. If something is late\, say
  it before you're asked\, with a real new time.\n\nBefore you go\, write t
 oday's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Try
 ing to look competent or likable makes people lie more. Your two fears\, f
 ailing and not being accepted\, are exactly these two goals. Week 2 teache
 s you to notice which one is running in the moment. (Feldman\, Forrest & H
 app (2002)\, Basic and Applied Social Psychology)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 37 Morning: Work
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
