SUMMARY:Day 38 Morning: Answer the whole question
DESCRIPTION:Week 6: Hard Truths. Tell the truth where it costs the most.\n
 \nWhen someone asks you something today\, especially at home\, answer it f
 ully the first time. A half-answer is a lie with better manners.\n\nHOW TO
  DO IT\n1. When someone asks you something today\, answer the whole questi
 on the first time.\n2. Before you answer\, ask yourself: "Is there a part 
 I'm leaving out that changes the picture?" If yes\, include it.\n3. Tonigh
 t\, go back and finish any half-answers you gave.\n\nBefore you go\, write
  today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: T
 rust after lying comes back slowly\, through actions. Set your expectation
 s: people believe you again slowly\, and words won't carry you. Answer ful
 ly the first time (Day 38) and keep small\, specific promises exactly (Day
  41). (Schweitzer\, Hershey & Bradlow (2006)\, Organizational Behavior and
  Human Decision Processes)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 38 Morning: Answer the whole question
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
