 whom\n2. Lies caught before I spoke (#)\n3. Corrections made (#)\n4. The t
 rigger: who\, where\, how tired I was\, and the fear (failure / rejection 
 / conflict / looking weak)\n5. The story in my head: "If I tell the truth\
 , ___ will happen."\n6. What actually happened when I told the truth\n7. T
 omorrow's risk moment\, written as an if-then: "If ___\, then I'll say ___
 ."\n8. One line of prayer or thanks
