SUMMARY:Day 39 Morning: Correct an old lie
DESCRIPTION:Week 6: Hard Truths. Tell the truth where it costs the most.\n
 \nPick one old lie that is still standing\, a small one\, and correct it: 
 "I told you ___. That wasn't true. The truth is ___."\n\nHOW TO DO IT\n1. 
 Pick one small old lie that's still standing\, one where the stakes are lo
 w.\n2. Plan your words: "I told you ___. That wasn't true. The truth is __
 _."\n3. Say it today\, without a long explanation.\n4. Tonight\, write the
  next old lie you want to correct.\n(Full instructions: "The correction" i
 n How to practice\, in your guide.)\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-th
 en: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Secrets weigh o
 n you even when nobody is asking. The lies you're still standing behind co
 st you every day\, not just when you're questioned. That's why Week 6 has 
 you start taking old lies down\, one at a time. (Slepian\, Chun & Mason (2
 017)\, Journal of Personality and Social Psychology)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 39 Morning: Correct an old lie
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
