DTEND:20270104T063500
SUMMARY:Day 40 Morning: No covering lies
DESCRIPTION:Week 6: Hard Truths. Tell the truth where it costs the most.\n
 \nWhen an old lie comes up today\, don't tell a new lie to protect it. If 
 you're not ready to correct it\, say nothing. Never add another layer.\n\n
 HOW TO DO IT\n1. Before you leave the house\, decide: if an old lie comes 
 up today\, you will not add a new lie to protect it.\n2. If you're not rea
 dy to correct it\, say nothing\, or say "I'd rather not get into that righ
 t now."\n3. Tonight\, note whether an old lie came up and what you did.\n\
 nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say __
 _."\n\nWhy it works: Small lies make bigger lies easier. There's no such t
 hing as a harmless small lie for you. Every exaggeration trains the slope.
  That's why Day 20 is "No rounding up." (Garrett\, Lazzaro\, Ariely & Shar
 ot (2016)\, Nature Neuroscience)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 40 Morning: No covering lies
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
