SUMMARY:Day 41 Morning: Keep one small promise
DESCRIPTION:Week 6: Hard Truths. Tell the truth where it costs the most.\n
 \nMake one small\, specific promise with a time on it\, and keep it exactl
 y.\n\nHOW TO DO IT\n1. Make one small promise to someone today with an exa
 ct time: "I'll call you back at 4."\n2. Set an alarm for it.\n3. Keep it e
 xactly\, on time.\n4. Tonight\, write whether you kept it. If you didn't\,
  correct it now: tell them and give a new time you will keep.\n\nBefore yo
 u go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy
  it works: Trust after lying comes back slowly\, through actions. Set your
  expectations: people believe you again slowly\, and words won't carry you
 . Answer fully the first time (Day 38) and keep small\, specific promises 
 exactly (Day 41). (Schweitzer\, Hershey & Bradlow (2006)\, Organizational 
 Behavior and Human Decision Processes)
