SUMMARY:Day 43 Morning: Your identity sentence
DESCRIPTION:Week 7: A Man Whose Word Holds. Not a streak. An identity.\n\n
 Rewrite your vision sentence: "I am a man who tells the truth when it cost
 s me." Read it three times this morning.\n\nHOW TO DO IT\n1. Write the sen
 tence on a card or your phone's lock screen: "I am a man who tells the tru
 th when it costs me."\n2. Read it out loud three times this morning.\n3. R
 ead it once more before any hard conversation today.\n\nBefore you go\, wr
 ite today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works
 : Remembering your values makes you less defensive. Before a hard truth\, 
 spend two minutes writing about what matters most to you: your faith\, you
 r children\, the man you've decided to be (Day 33). (Sherman & Cohen (2002
 )\, Current Directions in Psychological Science)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 43 Morning: Your identity sentence
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
