SUMMARY:Day 44 Morning: Your warning signs
DESCRIPTION:Week 7: A Man Whose Word Holds. Not a streak. An identity.\n\n
 Write your relapse warning signs: short on sleep\, stressed\, money troubl
 e\, skipping the ledger\, keeping "small" secrets\, rounding up again.\n\n
 HOW TO DO IT\n1. Read through your whole ledger from Day 1.\n2. List every
  pattern that came before your worst days: sleep\, stress\, money\, people
 \, places.\n3. Write these as your warning signs\, one per line.\n(Full in
 structions: "The nightly ledger" in How to practice\, in your guide.)\n\nB
 efore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___.
 "\n\nWhy it works: Tired men have less self-control. Treat being tired as 
 a risk factor. Your evening ledger and your relapse warning signs include 
 sleep. (Barnes\, Schaubroeck\, Huth & Ghumman (2011)\, Organizational Beha
 vior and Human Decision Processes)
