SUMMARY:Day 45 Morning: Your relapse plan
DESCRIPTION:Week 7: A Man Whose Word Holds. Not a streak. An identity.\n\n
 Write it and sign it: If I lie\, I will 1) correct it the same day\, 2) lo
 g it honestly\, 3) write myself two honest\, kind sentences instead of tea
 ring myself down\, 4) reread my if-then plans\, 5) keep going. I don't sta
 rt over at Day 1.\n\nHOW TO DO IT\n1. Write the relapse plan from the morn
 ing focus in your own handwriting.\n2. Sign and date it.\n3. Take a photo 
 and set it as a favorite\, or keep it in your wallet.\n4. Read it once ton
 ight.\n(Full instructions: "The correction" in How to practice\, in your g
 uide.)\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'
 ll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: A slip doesn't have to become a relapse. If 
 you lie\, you correct it\, log it\, and keep going. You never go back to D
 ay 1. (Marlatt & Gordon\, Relapse Prevention\; Larimer\, Palmer & Marlatt 
 (1999))
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 45 Morning: Your relapse plan
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
