SUMMARY:Day 46 Morning: A full honest day
DESCRIPTION:Week 7: A Man Whose Word Holds. Not a streak. An identity.\n\n
 Today is a test: go the whole day with zero lies. Use everything: the paus
 e\, "I don't know\," your if-then plans\, the 60-second correction.\n\nHOW
  TO DO IT\n1. Read all your if-then plans this morning.\n2. Count lies all
  day as you did on Day 1.\n3. Use every tool: the pause\, "I don't know\,"
  your if-then plans\, the 60-second correction.\n4. Tonight\, compare toda
 y's number with your Day 1 number.\n(Full instructions: "The three-second 
 pause" in How to practice\, in your guide.)\n\nBefore you go\, write today
 's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: If-then
  plans work. Every morning you write one if-then plan for the day's risk m
 oment: "If she asks about the money\, then I'll say the real number." (Gol
 lwitzer & Sheeran (2006)\, Advances in Experimental Social Psychology)
