SUMMARY:Day 48 Morning: Your ongoing system
DESCRIPTION:Week 7: A Man Whose Word Holds. Not a streak. An identity.\n\n
 Decide what keeps running after Day 49. Keep: the nightly ledger and the w
 eekly review. Optional: the morning if-then and the midday check.\n\nHOW T
 O DO IT\n1. Decide which practices continue: the nightly ledger and weekly
  review at minimum.\n2. Open Reminders and set them to repeat for the next
  90 days.\n3. Write one sentence about why you're continuing.\n\nBefore yo
 u go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy
  it works: You can do CBT on your own. Doing it alone works if you keep sh
 owing up. The daily reminders and the nightly ledger are your structure. T
 he biggest risk is quitting\, so the plan is built around never missing tw
 o nights in a row. (Karyotaki et al. (2017)\, JAMA Psychiatry)
